WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.792
Have you seen this

00:00:00.792 --> 00:00:01.918
bulletproof train

00:00:01.918 --> 00:00:03.503
that the North Korean dictator

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.504
is riding around in?

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.505
It's bulletproof.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:06.381
It's huge.

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:07.424
And it's what

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:08.883
the North Korean leader uses

00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:09.759
to leave the country

00:00:09.759 --> 00:00:11.136
because he's kind of afraid of flying.

00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:12.303
Or at least that's the rumor.

00:00:12.303 --> 00:00:12.846
Kim Jong-un

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.764
hasn't left the country in three years,

00:00:14.764 --> 00:00:16.349
but he just decided to do so.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.142
To go to Russia.

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:18.893
To visit President Vladimir Putin.

00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:20.645
He snaked up the coast of North Korea

00:00:20.645 --> 00:00:22.647
past this really bizarre place

00:00:22.647 --> 00:00:24.607
where China, Russia and North Korea borders

00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:25.525
all come together

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.901
and eventually made it to Eastern Russia.

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:27.277
By the way,

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:27.944
this train

00:00:27.944 --> 00:00:29.154
only goes like 30

00:00:29.154 --> 00:00:30.780
or 40 miles an hour max speed

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.824
because they want it to be extra safe.

00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:34.284
Kim is reportedly joined

00:00:34.284 --> 00:00:35.827
by his munitions and weapons

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:37.704
guy leading many experts to speculate

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.622
that this trip is about Russia

00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:41.666
asking North Korea for weapons.

00:00:41.666 --> 00:00:42.792
Reminder that Vladimir Putin

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:44.711
is very isolated from the world right now

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.671
and is struggling to get the weapons

00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:47.213
and materials

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.340
he needs to continue his war in Ukraine.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.508
So he's turning to a fellow

00:00:50.508 --> 00:00:52.260
outcast, North Korea, for help.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.511
So now we just wait and see

00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:54.596
if North Korean weapons

00:00:54.596 --> 00:00:55.972
start flowing into Russia.

00:00:55.972 --> 00:00:57.098
If you want to better understand

00:00:57.098 --> 00:00:59.059
global politics, follow for more.

